# Copy this file to .env.local for local development (.env.local is already
# covered by the project's blanket .env* .gitignore rule — never commit it).

# Base URL of clickscope-api. Must be reachable from the BROWSER, not just
# this machine's server process — every call in src/lib/api.ts runs
# client-side (the auth token lives in localStorage, unreadable from a
# Server Component; see Notes.md's "Server vs. client fetching" entry).
#
# This is why the var is prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_: Next.js only inlines
# NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed env vars into the client JavaScript bundle at build
# time. That prefix is a security boundary, not a naming convention — an
# unprefixed var is simply unavailable to client code (reads back as
# `undefined` at runtime, not a build error). If this var is missing,
# `fetch(`${undefined}/api/...`)` resolves to a relative URL against the
# Next.js dev server's own origin instead of clickscope-api, which 404s
# against Next's own (nonexistent) route rather than failing obviously.
#
# clickscope-api's own .env pins FRONTEND_URL/CORS_ORIGIN to
# http://localhost:5173 — that's why this repo's `npm run dev` runs on
# port 5173 (see package.json) instead of Next's default 3000, which the
# API itself already occupies.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
